 "summary": "Proof writing in this adaptation is robust and readable: three trailing `rfl`s and one bare `change` are eliminated, every new `change`/type ascription documents why no rewrite reaches the goal, and the Riemannian exponential gains a factored `hasFDerivAt` lemma instead of an `mfderiv_eq_fderiv` bridge. The measurability and `decide` adaptations close through named upstream lemmas (`eLpNorm_eq_eLpNorm'`, `lintegral_enorm_le_eLpNorm_one`, `cycleType_swap_mul_swap_of_nodup`) rather than brittle chains.",
